{
  "bridge_text": "既然你已经准备好听中文版的故事了，那就让我们回到莉娜站在寒冷田野上的那一刻，看看那棵树里究竟藏着什么秘密。",
  "resume_strategy": "restart",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "text": "在莉娜居住的那个羊毛灰色的村庄边缘，矗立着一棵比教堂还要高大的空心树。每个冬天的夜晚，树皮中都会飘出低沉的嗡嗡声，大人们总叮嘱：离那棵树远点。但那天晚上，当祖母在没讲完故事时就沉沉睡去，莉娜穿上那件红色的羊毛大衣，顶着寒风跨过冰霜覆盖的田野，决心去听听那声音到底在诉说着什么。"
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s1"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "The secret of Mosk's grumpiness hides in the shadows of the tree, but perhaps his heart will soften if Lina shows him kindness. Let us see what happens when she offers him a gift.",
  "resume_strategy": "continue",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "text": "Lina insisted she could not forget the song she had yet to hear, her eyes bright with curiosity. Mosk looked at her, his whiskers twitching as if he were deciding whether to scold her or simply let her be. The air inside the tree grew heavy with the scent of damp earth and old magic."
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "text": "Mosk pointed a shaky paw toward the door, his eyes narrow and stern. Lina reached into her pocket and pulled out the last apple of the season, setting it gently on the step between them. This is for the trouble of walking me down, she said softly. Mosk stared at the apple for a long time, his stern expression wavering. Then he stood up, pulled his vest tight, and stepped onto the first stair without another word."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s2"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "With Mosk the fox standing watch, the air in the hollow tree grew heavy with the secret he guarded. Lina looked past the grumpy guardian, wondering what else lay hidden in the deep roots.",
  "resume_strategy": "skip",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "text": "Mosk gestured sharply at the door, his eyes narrowing as he urged Lina to leave. She reached into her pocket and pulled out the last apple of the season, setting it gently on the wooden step between them. This is for the trouble of walking me down, she whispered. Mosk stared at the crisp fruit for a long time, his whiskers twitching. Without a word, he straightened his green vest and stepped onto the first stair, motioning for her to follow him into the dark."
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "text": "At the bottom of the stairs, the humming resolved into a soft, melodic song. A firefly as large as a robin lay curled on a bed of moss, her golden glow fading into a flicker. Mosk’s whiskers trembled as he looked down at her. She had been his friend once, he whispered, his voice cracking with a sorrow held for years. He had failed to bring her medicine during a harsh winter long ago, and he had been guarding this hollow ever since, too ashamed to face the light he had let dim."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s3"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "While Lina believed a kind gift might bridge the gap between them, the fox now stood ready to lead the way into the dark. Her apple sat on the step, a small hope offered in the silence.",
