{
  "bridge_text": "With that curious fox still watching her from the top step, Lina stood her ground. The air grew heavy with the secret of the humming, and Mosk seemed to weigh his next choice carefully.",
  "resume_strategy": "restart",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "text": "Inside the hollow tree, a narrow curl of stairs spiraled down into the dark. Perched on the very top step sat an old, grey fox wearing a vest stitched together with patches of green. His name was Mosk. He spoke in a raspy voice, like dry leaves skittering across stone, warning Lina that the tree was no place for a visitor and that she should return home at once. But Lina shook her head, insisting that she could not possibly forget a sound she had yet to truly hear."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s2"
