{
  "bridge_text": "Just as Mosk kept his heavy stone of regret hidden from view, he now chose to share his long-silent voice with the queen. The forest seemed to hold its breath as the melody blossomed.",
  "resume_strategy": "restart",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "text": "Lina knelt to ask the firefly queen what she needed, and the queen whispered that a drop of warm milk and a kind word were the oldest medicines of all. Mosk carefully fetched the milk in a tiny thimble, his paw trembling slightly as he laid it beside Lina’s hand. As the queen’s soft glow finally steadied, the humming inside the hollow tree shifted into a beautiful, forgotten tune. Mosk, who had carried his secret shame like a heavy stone for so many years, finally let his guard down and hummed along, his voice weaving perfectly with the queen's song."
    }
  ],
